   "fix": "Move all four into `TauCeti/Topology/Homotopy/Cube/Basic.lean` under the `TauCeti` namespace, next to `piOptionEquivProdHomeomorph_symm_mem_boundary` and `Cube.mk_mem_prodBoundary`. Make them public, give them docstrings, and import them from `Exact.lean`.",
   "issue": "Four helpers are made `private` here instead of being placed where they belong: `genLoopOfProd`/`genLoopOfProd_apply` (a map `I \u00d7 I^N \u2192 X` that is `x` on `prodBoundary` read as `\u03a9^(Option N)`), `apply_symm_of_mem_prodBoundary` (a generalized loop on `I^(Option N)` equals its basepoint at `\u03c6.symm y` for `y \u2208 prodBoundary`), `update_symm_some` (`Function.update` commutes with `piOptionEquivProdHomeomorph.symm`), and `update_mem_boundary` (`Cube.boundary` is preserved by updating a coordinate from an endpoint to an endpoint). None of them uses fibrations; they are general facts about `I^(Option N) \u2243 I \u00d7 I^N` and `Cube.boundary`.",
   "line": 0
  }
